  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 142 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nTonight through next Wednesday\n\nTonight - Sunday:\n\nRain and storm chances will continue to decrease for majority of the \nCWA as the frontal boundary traverse south this afternoon. Once the \nfront stalls near the Gulf coastline, evening rain chances will\nbecome confined to the Pine Belt through the early evening. The \ntrough will lift northward Friday, allowing an upper-lvl high over\nthe Southwest & Texas to gradually move eastward towards the \nSoutheast. Patchy fog development may be possible pre-sunrise \nFriday morning. A cut-off low pressure near Gulf states will track\nwestwards, shifting rain chances southeast into the Pine Belt \ninto weekend, with the Interstate 59 corridor ranging from 15-30% \nFriday through Sunday. As the high progresses, heat indices are \nexpected start increasing to near 100 degrees by Sunday.\n\nMonday - Wednesday Night:\n\nThe aforementioned high will settle over the Southeast CONUS around \nTuesday, lingering through the rest of the week. As a result, \ndangerous heat concerns are expected to return mid-week as heat \nindices peak near or in excess of 105F. HWO graphics may be needed \nbut timing is still several days aways. Another low pressure will \ntraverse around the ridge, bring deep moisture and storm chances \nsoutheast of I-20 and along HWY 84 through the forecast \nperiod. /SW/DC/",
